# TryHackMe SOC Simulator — Phishing Investigation

## Introduction

This write-up documents my investigation of a phishing-related alert from the **TryHackMe SOC Simulator — Introduction to Phishing** scenario.

The investigation was performed using **Splunk** as the SIEM to analyze email and firewall telemetry. The objective was to determine whether an inbound email represented a genuine phishing attempt or legitimate business activity, establish whether the recipient interacted with the embedded URL, and determine whether escalation was required.

> **Final Verdict:** False Positive
> **Escalation:** Not Required
> **Affected User:** Julia Garcia

---

## Investigation Objective

The alert required me to:

* Analyze the suspicious email.
* Identify the sender, recipient, URL, and other indicators.
* Determine whether the URL was accessed.
* Correlate email activity with firewall logs.
* Determine whether the activity represented malicious behavior.
* Identify the affected endpoint.
* Decide whether the alert was a True Positive or False Positive.
* Determine whether escalation was required.
* Document the investigation in a case report.

